0..77 Comment "// The circle and the integers without a higher inductive type. The circle is"
78..153 Comment "// presented by a point, a loop and its inverse, with the two cancellations"
154..228 Comment "// as rules; its shape is a signature, and the integers are a model of it."
229..303 Comment "// The winding number, written as a bare `case`, is refused until the fold"
304..373 Comment "// into the integers lands, and the equivalence between them is owed."
375..452 Comment "/// The circle as a presented type: its rules rewrite constructor terms, so a"
453..495 Comment "/// word normalizes to the loops it winds."
